      "text": "To convert from rectangular coordinates \\((x, y, z) = (0, -3\\sqrt{3}, 3)\\) to spherical coordinates \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi)\\), we use the following formulas:\n\n1. \\(\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2}\\)\n2. \\(\\theta = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)\\) (with consideration of the quadrant)\n3. \\(\\phi = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{z}{\\rho}\\right)\\)\n\nLet's calculate each step.\n\nFirst, calculate \\(\\rho\\):\n\\[\n\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2} = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-3\\sqrt{3})^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{0 + 27 + 9} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(\\theta\\):\n\\[\n\\theta = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right) = \\arctan\\left(\\frac{-3\\sqrt{3}}{0}\\right)\n\\]\nSince \\(x = 0\\) and \\(y = -3\\sqrt{3}\\), the point \\((0, -3\\sqrt{3}, 3)\\) lies on the negative \\(y\\)-axis. Therefore, \\(\\theta\\) is:\n\\[\n\\theta = \\frac{3\\pi}{2}\n\\]\n\nFinally, calculate \\(\\phi\\):\n\\[\n\\phi = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{z}{\\rho}\\right) = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{3}{6}\\right) = \\arccos\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the spherical coordinates are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(6, \\frac{3\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{3})}\n\\]",
